{{!
    @template enrol_apply/queue_view

    The approval queue of one method as a data report, read only (stage 3): one mount point, today's
    queue for a browser without JavaScript, and the way back to today's table.

    The mount names the bundle (js/esm/bundle.json), as enrol_apply/report_view does; its props name
    the queue's view in "mount". Its inner content is what the first paint shows until React commits:
    a skeleton in the shape of the tiles and the grid and, hidden behind it, one sentence that is true
    only if the component never mounts, swapped by styles.css about 10 s after the first paint.

    The props arrive already JSON-encoded by enrol_apply\output\queue_view, in one value, through a
    triple stash: nothing between here and React is an HTML context. They carry configuration and
    strings, never an application.

    The link to the table carries the filters in the address; the client keeps its href in step with
    the address as the reader changes them (data-enrol-apply-queue="tablelink").

    Context variables required for this template:
    * props - the component's props, JSON.
    * tableurl - manage.php with the same filters and no view parameter.
    * noscript - today's queue, HTML.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "props": "{\"mount\": \"queue\", \"enrolid\": 3, \"labels\": {\"loading\": \"Loading applications\"}}",
        "tableurl": "https://example.com/enrol/apply/manage.php?id=3",
        "noscript": "<p>Today's queue</p>"
    }
}}
<div class="enrol_apply-rview enrol_apply-qview" data-enrol-apply-queue="view">
    <p class="enrol_apply-rview-tablelink">
        <a href="{{tableurl}}" data-enrol-apply-queue="tablelink">{{#str}}reportviewtableview, enrol_apply{{/str}}</a>
    </p>
    {{#react}}
    {
        "component": "@moodle/lms/enrol_apply/bundle",
        "props": {{{props}}},
        "class": "enrol_apply-rview-mount"
    }
    <div class="enrol_apply-rview-preload" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="enrol_apply-rview-band">
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
            <div class="enrol_apply-rview-tile enrol_apply-rview-sk"><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span><span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb enrol_apply-rview-skb--big"></span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="enrol_apply-rview-skgrid enrol_apply-rview-sk">
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
            <span class="enrol_apply-rview-skb"></span>
        </div>
    </div>
    <p class="enrol_apply-rview-failed">{{#str}}queueviewmountfailed, enrol_apply{{/str}}</p>
    {{/react}}
    <noscript>{{{noscript}}}</noscript>
</div>
